//? Title: Principal Components: Variance, Projection and Kernel Centring
//? Subtitle: Fit the centre once and preserve it for every new query batch
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Correlated measurements can be represented in fewer orthogonal coordinates, but projection
must use a fixed training centre and scale. We recover the known axes of four points, check
variance lost by a rank-one reconstruction and check linear Gram and covariance spectra. A built-in
Iris example then illustrates descriptive covariance geometry.
)
\toc

> The method

After centring the data matrix X, its thin SVD X=USVᵀ gives orthonormal axes V and scores US.
The sample covariance eigenvalues are s_j²/(N-1). Keeping q leading components minimises
squared reconstruction error over rank-q orthogonal projections:

$$
\|X-XV_qV_q^T\|_F^2=\sum_{j>q}s_j^2.
$$
\alttext(The total squared rank-q reconstruction residual is the sum of discarded squared singular values.)

The report fits a unit direction with explicit tensor SGD and a two-axis subspace with
explicit tensor Adam. In the latter, differentiable QR maps unconstrained weights to
orthonormal columns at every step; QR does not supply the data-dependent optimum.
The reconstruction loss is that of a tied linear autoencoder. SVD is used only to
check the final minimum. Learned axes may rotate within the same principal subspace,
so compare reconstruction error rather than individual vector signs. Each objective
evaluation costs O(NDq), plus O(Dq²) for its QR constraint.

The optimum follows by rotating into V coordinates, where the Frobenius norm separates into squared
column norms. Scaling predictors changes covariance PCA to correlation PCA; the toy uses unscaled data, while Iris uses tensor-computed sample standard deviations. Kernel PCA instead centres a Gram
matrix K with H=I-11ᵀ/N and diagonalises HKH. Its eigenvalues are Gram eigenvalues, not sample
variances; divide by N-1 to compare with covariance PCA. Query centring must use training means,
not each query batch's own mean. No input-space inverse is claimed for kernel PCA.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/principal_components_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/principal_components_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/principal_components_concept.tikz > build/principal_components_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/principal_components_concept.svg build/principal_components_concept.dvi > build/principal_components_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/principal_components_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
